:: Loft Smoke
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<if $whitney_smoke is undefined>><<set $whitney_smoke to 0>><</if>>
<<set $cigarettes -= 1>><<pass 5>><<wearProp "cigarette">>
You ease one of the loft windows open and sit on the sill, keeping most of your body inside. The forest air comes straight through the gap, so you lean towards it whenever you breathe out. That should keep the smoke away from the rafters where the other orphans like to hide.
<br><br>
<<if $whitney_smoke lt 3>>
	You hold the cigarette between your fingers and try the lighter twice before the flame stays on. The first drag burns your throat, and you press your lips together to stop yourself coughing.
<<elseif $whitney_smoke lt 7>>
	You shield the lighter from the draught and light the tip. The first drag still stings a little, though nowhere near as badly as it used to.
<<else>>
	You light the cigarette without much thought, take a deep drag, then breathe the smoke out over the garden below.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Keep going|Loft Smoke Mid]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Loft Smoke Mid
<<effects>><<pass 2>>
<<if $loft_whitney gte 6 and !Time.schoolTime and !$weekly.loftSmokeWhitney and random(1,100) lt 45>>
	<<set $weekly.loftSmokeWhitney to true>>
	You're halfway through, smoke curling lazy from the corner of your mouth,
	when something small cracks off the window frame beside your head and skitters away across the floor.
	<br><br>
	A pebble.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Look down|Loft Smoke Whitney]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<cleareventpool>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_forest" 1>>
		You rest your forearms on the sill and breathe the smoke towards the trees. The noise from downstairs feels far away up here, giving you a few quiet minutes to yourself.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_ash" 1>>
		Ash gathers at the tip. You tap it outside and watch the grey bits disappear before they reach the garden.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_orphans" 1>>
		Two orphans start arguing somewhere in the garden below. You can hear them from here, but you keep smoking and leave them to sort it out themselves.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_whitney_memory" 1>>
		The taste makes you think of Whitney: the cocky tilt of <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> head, the cigarette usually hanging from <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> lips, and the way <<nnpc_he "Whitney">> looks around before deciding where to stand. You take another drag and turn your attention back to the forest.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_window" 1>>
		You shift your hips on the sill and keep the cigarette outside. No smoke gets into the loft, and none of the orphans below seem to notice what you're doing.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_quiet" 1>>
		After a few drags, your shoulders drop and you stop shifting around on the sill. You stay where you are and let the cigarette burn down between your fingers.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_bird" 1>>
		A bird lands on the gutter beside you and turns its head towards the cigarette. When you breathe smoke away from it, it hops back once before flying off.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_breeze" 1>>
		A gust pushes the smoke back towards your face. You turn away, wait for the clean air to reach you again, then carry on.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_sky" 1>>
		<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
			The orange tip stands out against the dark garden below. Each drag makes it glow brighter before it fades again.
		<<elseif Time.dayState is "dusk">>
			The sun is dropping behind the trees. You take another drag while the last orange light fades over the garden.
		<<else>>
			The garden is bright below you. Each breath of smoke shows clearly in the daylight before the breeze carries it over the trees.
		<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_weather" 2>>
		<<if Weather.bloodMoon and Time.dayState is "night">>
			The moon is red above the forest, and its light colours the tops of the trees. You stare until your arms prickle, then take another drag and rub your thumb along the paper before looking down at the garden instead.
		<<elseif Weather.name is "thunderstorm">>
			Rain blows through the open window when thunder rolls over the forest. You pull the cigarette under the edge of the roof, keeping the lit tip dry while lightning flashes beyond the trees.
		<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
			Rain taps against the sill. You keep the cigarette near the window frame and turn it away whenever the wind blows drops inside.
		<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
			Snow falls past the window and melts when a flake lands on the lit tip. Your breath mixes with the smoke each time you breathe out.
		<<elseif Weather.isOvercast>>
			The sky is grey above the forest. You rest against the frame and watch the smoke fade into it.
		<<else>>
			The air is still, so the smoke rises above the window before the breeze carries it towards the trees.
		<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_season" 2>>
		<<if Time.season is "winter">>
			The cold soon gets into your fingers. You swap the cigarette between hands, warming the free one against your clothes before taking another drag.
		<<elseif Time.season is "spring">>
			Birds call from the forest below, and the air smells of wet earth and blossom. The cigarette tastes harsher beside it, but you keep smoking anyway.
		<<elseif Time.season is "summer">>
			Warm air comes through the window carrying the smell of dry grass. You lean further out and let the smoke drift away from the loft.
		<<else>>
			Dead leaves blow past the window whenever the wind picks up. You watch them tumble over the garden while you smoke.
		<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_drag" 1>>
		You take another drag, slower this time, then let the smoke out through your nose. The burn doesn't bother you as much as it used to.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_stress" 1>>
		You notice you've stopped clenching your jaw. Whatever was bothering you earlier is still there, but you're not thinking about it quite as hard now.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_lean" 1>>
		You rest your cheek against the cool window frame and let one leg hang outside, slowly turning the cigarette between your fingers.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_haze" 1>>
		Your head feels a little light when you move it too quickly. You stay against the frame until the feeling settles.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_alone" 1>>
		Nobody calls your name from downstairs. You stay by the window, smoke in peace, and enjoy having nothing else to do for a few minutes.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<runeventpool>>
	<br><br>
	<<smokeicon>><<link [[Finish the cigarette|Loft Smoke Finish]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Stub it out half-finished|Loft Smoke Stop]]>><<set $phase to "drop">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Loft Smoke Finish
<<effects>><<pass 2>><<smokeApply>>
<<if _smokeOutcome is "passout">>
	By the time you finish another cigarette in quick succession, your head is already swimming. A cold sweat breaks across your neck, and when you try to straighten up your legs give way beneath you.
	<br><br>
	<span class="red">You've overdone it.</span> Your hand slips from the window frame.<<gggstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Loft Smoke Passout]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You smoke down to the filter, take one last drag, then press the stub against the brick outside until the ember dies. You drop it away from the window.
	<br><br>
	<<if _smokeOutcome is "woozy">>
		Taking two so close together makes you feel dizzy and a little sick. You feel slightly less tired,
		but more on edge.<<gstress>><<ltiredness>><<ghallucinogens>>
	<<else>>
		You relax as you breathe out the smoke. The herb leaves you feeling pleasantly light, and a little less tired.<<lstress>><<ltiredness>><<ghallucinogens>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if ($daily.cigarettesSmoked ?? 0) gte 5>>
		<span class="blue">That's five today. Any more and your chest would punish you for it; you've had enough.</span>
		<br>
	<<elseif $cigarettes gte 1>>
		<<smokeicon>><<link [[Light another|Loft Smoke]]>><</link>> | <span class="gold">(<<= $cigarettes>> left)</span>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<span class="blue">That was your last one.</span>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Climb back inside|Loft Smoke Stop]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Loft Smoke Stop
<<effects>>
<<if $phase is "drop">>
	You press the half-smoked cigarette against the brick until the tip goes dark, then drop the stub outside. You're done smoking for now.
<<elseif $hallucinations gte 2>>
	You pull yourself off the sill and put both feet on the floor before closing the window. Your balance still feels a little off, so you keep one hand on the frame for a moment.
<<else>>
	You take one last breath of the forest air, swing your legs back inside, then close the window behind you.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Orphanage Loft]]>><<endevent>><<handheldon>><</link>>
<br>

:: Loft Smoke Passout
<<effects>>
<<if $smokeReturn is undefined>><<set $smokeReturn to "Orphanage Loft">><</if>>
<<set $cigaretteChain to 0>>
<<if $smokePlace is "loft" or $smokeReturn is "Orphanage Loft">>
	Your knees give way, and you slide down the wall beneath the window. Your vision fades to grey, then black.
<<else>>
	Your knees buckle where you stand. You reach for something to steady yourself, miss, and crumple to the ground as your sight turns grey.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<passout>><<pass 90>>
<<if $smokePlace is "loft" or $smokeReturn is "Orphanage Loft">>
	You wake on the loft floor with your back against the wall, head pounding and mouth dry. A couple of orphans stand nearby whispering about whether they should fetch Bailey, but they hurry off when they see you move.
<<else>>
	You wake where you fell, head pounding and mouth dry. Nobody stayed to help, though someone has moved around you rather than stepping over you.
<</if>>
You won't be reaching for another cigarette any time soon.<<gtrauma>><<trauma 3>>
<br><br>
<<link "Next" $smokeReturn>><</link>>
<br>

:: Loft Smoke Whitney
<<endevent>><<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<npc Whitney>><<person1>>
/* The ordinary loft finish applies this after the last drag. This branch leaves that flow halfway through, so record the cigarette here instead. */
<<smokeDependence>><<set $daily.cigarettesSmoked to ($daily.cigarettesSmoked ?? 0) + 1>>
You lean further out and look down. Whitney is standing in the garden with another pebble in <<his>> hand, grinning when <<he>> sees you looking.
<br><br>
"Hey, <<slut>>!" <<he>> calls up, not bothering to keep <<his>> voice down.
"Enjoying your smoke break up there, all cosy and quiet? The fuck's this, you got your own private balcony now?"
<br><br>
<<He>> spreads <<his>> arms wide. "Well? You gonna leave me standing down here like a goddamn delivery bastard,
or you gonna get me up there? Throw down a rope, a sheet, that creaky little winch of yours, I don't give a shit.
Just get me up!"
<br><br>
<<link [[Lower the winch|Loft Smoke Whitney Up]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Tease Whitney about the winch|Loft Smoke Whitney Tease]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Loft Smoke Whitney Tease
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
You lean a little further out and rest your chin on your hand.
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"That old winch? I dunno, Whitney. It's rated for baskets of sweets, not whatever you've been eating.
	Reckon it'll snap the second it takes your fat head." You sneer.
	<br><br>
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant">>
		You give the handle a theatrical turn, making the cable creak. "Very reassuring."
	<<else>>
		You tap a bit of ash outside, nowhere near <<him>>, but <<he>> still looks offended.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	"I'm just saying, that winch was built to haul up chocolates. You're a fair bit heavier than a bag of sweets.
	Sure it'll hold?" you ask.
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		Even as you say it, you pull the handle towards you and start getting the line ready.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
		You try to hide your smile behind the cigarette when <<he>> glares up at you.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite">>
		"I'd rather not explain to Bailey why you fell off the wall."
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
Whitney's grin disappears. <<He>> raises both middle fingers at the window.
"Oh, real fucking funny, <<bitch>>! I'm wounded! Now quit running your mouth and
HURRY THE FUCK UP before I climb the wall myself and throw you off it!"
<br><br>
<<link [[Lower the winch|Loft Smoke Whitney Up]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Loft Smoke Whitney Up
<<effects>>
You haul the winch line over and pay it out down the wall. Whitney grabs hold, plants a boot against the brick,
and the old wire groans the whole way up while <<he>> curses every centimetre of it.
When <<his>> head clears the sill <<he>> hooks an elbow over the frame and drags <<himself>> in,
dropping into the loft beside you.
<br><br>
"See? Held just fine." <<He>> brushes brick dust off <<his>> front,
then looks at the cigarette still smouldering in your hand and snorts. "Course you'd find the one window in this
dump nobody checks. Smart, for a slut."
<br><br>
<<He>> drops into a crouch against the wall, take out a battered packet out of <<his>> pocket,
and tosses it so it lands in your hand, which you reflexively catch. <<His>> own.
The corner's crushed and the lid's soft from handling.
<br><br>
"Smoke one with me." It isn't really a question, the way <<he>> says it.
"Don't make me sit up here looking like an idiot on my own."
<br><br>
<<link [[Smoke with Whitney|Loft Smoke Whitney Together]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Refuse|Loft Smoke Whitney Refuse]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Loft Smoke Whitney Refuse
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
	"Not right now," you say, holding the packet out without looking up. "I just don't feel like another."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You hesitate with the packet in your hand, then offer it back. "Not right now.
	Sorry. You can stay, though."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Not right now, thanks." You pass the packet back.
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant">>
		"You climbed all this way for company, though. I'm not throwing you straight back out."
	<</if>>
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	You hand the packet back. "Not right now. Smoke yours if you want."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	You push the packet back into <<his>> hand. "Smoke your own. I'm done."
<<else>>
	You hold the packet back out to <<him>>. "Not right now."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Whitney stops smiling. <<He>> takes the packet back and shoves it into <<his>> pocket.
<br><br>
"Tch. Suit yourself, then. The fuck did I climb up here for." <<He>> still doesn't leave. Instead, <<he>> sits deeper in the corner by the window, takes out one of <<his>> own and lights it.
"Stand there and watch. See if I care, you cold <<bitch>>."<<npcincr Whitney love -2>><<llove>>
<br><br>
Whitney pulls <<his>> knees up and smokes in silence, staring out at the trees. Every so often <<he>> glances your way, but <<he>> makes no move towards the window.
<br><br>
<<set $daily.loftSmokeCorner to true>>
<<link [[Leave Whitney to it|Orphanage Loft]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Loft Smoke Whitney Together
<<effects>><<wearProp "cigarette">>
<<if !$daily.loftWhitneyPack>><<set $cigarettes += 4>><<set $daily.loftWhitneyPack to true>><</if>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"Okay," you say, taking one from the packet.
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
		You keep your eyes on the cigarette while Whitney moves beside you.
	<</if>>
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"All right," you say, taking one as soon as <<he>> offers the packet.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Since you climbed all the way up here," you say, taking a cigarette.
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant">>
		"You'd be unbearable if I sent you home disappointed."
	<</if>>
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Fine. Light it for me," you say, putting the cigarette between your lips.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Only because watching you sulk on your own would be pathetic," you say, taking one.
<<else>>
	"Sure," you say, taking a cigarette.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Whitney moves beside you at the sill until <<his>> shoulder rests against yours. <<He>> shields the lighter with one hand and holds the flame to your cigarette, waiting until the tip glows before lighting <<his>> own.
<br><br>
For a while, neither of you talks. You smoke with your elbows on the sill, listening to the orphanage below and the occasional creak of the old window.
<br><br>
With nobody else around, Whitney stops running <<his>> mouth. <<His>> shoulders relax, and after a while <<he>> just watches the forest with you. You glance sideways at <<him>> a few times before <<he>> turns and spots you doing it.
<br><br>
"Oi. Look at this, slut."
Whitney takes a deep drag, rounds <<his>> lips, then taps <<his>> cheek twice. A row of smoke rings leaves <<his>> mouth and hangs outside the window before the breeze breaks them apart. <<He>> looks at you with a smug grin.
"Your turn."
<br><br>
<<link [[Try to do it too|Loft Smoke Whitney Shapes]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Loft Smoke Whitney Shapes
<<effects>>
<<if $whitney_smoke gte 7>>
	You've practised this by now. You keep the smoke in your mouth, move your tongue the way Whitney showed you, then tap your cheek. Three clean rings leave your lips, and the last passes through the first before the wind breaks them apart.
	<br><br>
	Whitney's eyebrows jump. "Oh, you little show-off." <<He>> laughs before <<he>> can stop <<himself>>.
	"Where'd a <<slut>> like you learn to do that, huh? Fucking copycat."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> tries to look unimpressed, but the colour in <<his>> cheeks gives <<him>> away. "Yeah, yeah. Not bad.
	Don't let it go to your head."<<npcincr Whitney love 2>><<gglove>><<npcincr Whitney lust 5>>
<<else>>
	You take some smoke into your mouth and try to copy <<him>>, tapping your cheek the same way. Instead of forming a ring, the smoke goes straight down your throat. You bend over the sill coughing while your eyes water.<<pain 5>><<gpain>>
	<br><br>
	Whitney laughs so hard <<he>> has to put a hand on the wall. "Pfff, holy shit. That was pathetic. You looked like you were dying,
	slut." <<He>> wipes under one eye as though <<he>> has laughed himself to tears.
	<br><br>
	Even while <<he>> is taking the piss, <<his>> other hand settles on your lower back and rubs slowly until you can breathe properly again. "There, there. Breathe, dumbass.
	Your body's just gotta learn how to take it. You're used to that, right?"
	<<set $whitney_smoke += 1>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Loft Smoke Whitney Menu]]>><</link>>
<br>

